WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:02.965
- Once all the Christmas
songs start coming on

00:00:02.965 --> 00:00:04.362
the first thing I can think of is

00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:06.387
when are we gonna get to January second,

00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:08.337
like can this all be over soon.

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:09.325
- Hi.

00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:11.627
I'm Matt, and my parents got divorced

00:00:11.627 --> 00:00:13.157
when I was eight years old.

00:00:13.157 --> 00:00:14.983
Now I know no two divorces are the same.

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:17.665
But if there's any time
of year that unifies

00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:21.073
people with divorced
parents, it's the holidays.

00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:23.718
And the fact that they're
pretty complicated.

00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:25.857
So I asked some of my
coworkers with divorced parents

00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:27.933
to share some of their experiences

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:29.903
and feelings towards the holiday season.

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:32.334
And how it's changed
from when they were kids,

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.751
to now as adults.

00:00:36.551 --> 00:00:38.507
- I'm Logan, my parents got divorced

00:00:38.507 --> 00:00:40.189
when I was about five years old.

00:00:40.189 --> 00:00:43.206
- I'm Jamie, I'm 27, my parents

00:00:43.206 --> 00:00:44.774
divorced when I was five.

00:00:44.774 --> 00:00:46.993
- Hi my name's Lindsey, I was 21

00:00:46.993 --> 00:00:48.483
when my parents got divorced.

00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:51.838
- My name's Alp, I am
currently 27 years old,

00:00:51.838 --> 00:00:55.147
and I was six years old when
my parents got divorced.

00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:58.801
- So I'm Emily, I was four
when my parents got divorced.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:02.818
- I'm Chelsea, my parents got
divorced, when I was like,

00:01:02.818 --> 00:01:06.275
oh they got separated when
I was like eight or nine,

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.629
and then didn't officially
get divorced til

00:01:09.629 --> 00:01:12.719
I was 15 cause shit's messy.

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:15.417
- I don't really remember
them together at all,

00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:18.173
which means I only really
know spending Christmas

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.833
with both of them, meaning
I had two Christmases.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.320
- It never really affected Christmas,

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.653
other than the fact that I
had a lot of extra presents.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.310
- Now that they're divorced, I'm an adult,

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.867
the holidays are extremely inconvenient.

00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:34.699
- In a weird way I feel
fortunate because I was so young

00:01:34.699 --> 00:01:36.961
and you know when you're that age,

00:01:36.961 --> 00:01:39.886
like things don't feel weird,
that's just your family.

00:01:39.886 --> 00:01:41.421
And that's just your day to day life.

00:01:41.421 --> 00:01:43.772
- The holidays were weird because,

00:01:43.772 --> 00:01:47.336
like I didn't have memories
from when they were together,

00:01:47.336 --> 00:01:49.288
so I always thought that people would

00:01:49.288 --> 00:01:52.621
go to one house one year and
then another house another year

00:01:52.621 --> 00:01:54.680
and then I grew up and was like wait...

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.823
- The biggest thing I think in retrospect

00:01:56.823 --> 00:02:00.782
that like I really wanted to
do was maintain traditions.

00:02:00.782 --> 00:02:02.836
I do have memories of being like,

00:02:02.836 --> 00:02:06.736
well my dad's not part
of the Christmas anymore,

00:02:06.736 --> 00:02:08.831
who's gonna fill my mom's stocking

00:02:08.831 --> 00:02:11.188
and give her like, pajamas
and Santa presents.

00:02:11.188 --> 00:02:14.295
- As you get older having
divorced parents sucks.

00:02:14.295 --> 00:02:16.638
Because you essentially
have to pick one parent.

00:02:16.638 --> 00:02:18.683
- I have had a lot of step
parents over the years,

00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:20.478
five to be exact.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.460
- So just rolling between, two households,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.200
driving and staying sober at one or the other,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.572
which is hard enough as it
is without divorced parents.

00:02:29.572 --> 00:02:32.131
- It's always better to
have more support around you

00:02:32.131 --> 00:02:33.645
growing up as a child I think,

00:02:33.645 --> 00:02:37.701
but I was really happy
that they were both happy.

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.295
- Now I kind of don't like the holidays,

00:02:39.295 --> 00:02:41.389
because it makes me feel tired I guess.

00:02:41.389 --> 00:02:43.338
- If you're dating or in a relationship

00:02:43.338 --> 00:02:45.416
with someone who also
has divorced parents,

00:02:45.416 --> 00:02:47.749
it really sucks cause
then you have four parents

00:02:47.749 --> 00:02:49.753
to deal with and you
essentially have to choose

00:02:49.753 --> 00:02:51.581
one of them and you
feel like you're always

00:02:51.581 --> 00:02:54.240
gonna hurt someone's feelings essentially.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.316
- When I was growing up we had like,

00:02:56.316 --> 00:03:00.316
exciting, fun, big holidays,
big Italian family,

00:03:02.071 --> 00:03:03.934
everyone in one place usually,

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:07.337
in my parent's home, so
now that's different.

00:03:07.337 --> 00:03:08.920
And a lot less fun.

00:03:09.818 --> 00:03:13.423
- One thing that is cool,
about having two separate

00:03:13.423 --> 00:03:15.792
families during the holidays is that

00:03:15.792 --> 00:03:18.478
you get to spend a lot of
time with your siblings

00:03:18.478 --> 00:03:20.907
kind of bonding over the
shared weird experience

00:03:20.907 --> 00:03:22.466
that you're all going through.

00:03:22.466 --> 00:03:26.277
- It like started being
okay when we just kind of

00:03:26.277 --> 00:03:29.610
stopped trying to combine it in any way.

00:03:31.412 --> 00:03:34.291
And I'd have like lunch
or something with my dad.

00:03:34.291 --> 00:03:38.059
- If you have siblings
it's just a giant mess.

00:03:38.059 --> 00:03:40.536
So when you're young it's
cool to have two Christmases,

00:03:40.536 --> 00:03:43.279
but as you get older, it
becomes really complicated.

00:03:43.279 --> 00:03:45.942
- I actually love Christmas,
I've never disliked it.

00:03:45.942 --> 00:03:49.502
I put my tree up two days
after Thanksgiving, this year.

00:03:49.502 --> 00:03:53.701
But I haven't spent Christmas
with family since 2009.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:57.459
- Yeah it is a little
weird to juggle your time.

00:03:57.459 --> 00:04:01.051
And keeping two sides
of the family separate,

00:04:01.051 --> 00:04:04.278
so I don't know, I guess
it is normal to feel like,

00:04:04.278 --> 00:04:07.861
you have to sacrifice
your personal desires

00:04:09.235 --> 00:04:11.936
to do things that are right
for your family members

00:04:11.936 --> 00:04:13.837
and everybody's comfortable in the space.

00:04:13.837 --> 00:04:15.932
- When you're a kid you're
just super sheltered,

00:04:15.932 --> 00:04:19.087
and you, again, just don't
really realize what's not normal.

00:04:19.087 --> 00:04:21.762
So I think growing up
that kind of clicked.

00:04:21.762 --> 00:04:23.742
Being like oh I don't
have to do this anymore.

00:04:23.742 --> 00:04:27.046
I don't have to spend all my
time worrying about family

00:04:27.046 --> 00:04:29.628
matters and all that
stuff, and I guess I just

00:04:29.628 --> 00:04:31.772
chose to be indifferent
about the holidays.

00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:33.931
- I could just like
ignore all the problems

00:04:33.931 --> 00:04:36.493
if we just separated it and
weren't trying to bounce around.

00:04:36.493 --> 00:04:38.467
- The holidays now are
kinda like a mixed bag

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.597
because it's kinda nice
to see parents that

00:04:40.597 --> 00:04:42.140
you don't see all the
time when you're an adult.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.346
Especially if you don't live
in the same state as them.

00:04:44.346 --> 00:04:46.912
But it really just becomes
a scheduling nightmare

00:04:46.912 --> 00:04:48.531
trying to figure out things cause

00:04:48.531 --> 00:04:49.706
you don't get a lot of time off,

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:50.970
but you wanna see your parents.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.616
- I have a good
relationship with my family.

00:04:52.616 --> 00:04:54.095
I call them I talk to them.

00:04:54.095 --> 00:04:57.428
But we're not very celebratory together.

00:04:58.323 --> 00:05:01.157
- The general feeling I
have of my parents divorce

00:05:01.157 --> 00:05:04.702
is a feeling of like, I
feel it was the right thing.

00:05:04.702 --> 00:05:09.572
And I think I benefited
growing up from that choice.

00:05:09.572 --> 00:05:12.031
- I don't know, it's hard,
it's complicated I guess.

00:05:12.031 --> 00:05:14.864
I think as an adult, I, feel like,

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:20.644
especially cause I live
3,000 miles away from home,

00:05:20.644 --> 00:05:24.203
and so when I go home I wanna see

00:05:24.203 --> 00:05:26.379
also my friends and balancing that

00:05:26.379 --> 00:05:29.633
with seeing like my extended family.

00:05:29.633 --> 00:05:31.678
- You kind of feel like
a child at some times

00:05:31.678 --> 00:05:33.890
cause it's like well I
was with mom last year,

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.586
this year I have to be with dad.

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:38.119
- Once all the Christmas
songs start coming on

00:05:38.119 --> 00:05:39.688
the first thing I can think of is

00:05:39.688 --> 00:05:41.395
when are we gonna get to January second,

00:05:41.395 --> 00:05:43.504
like can this all be over soon.

00:05:43.504 --> 00:05:46.410
- I've always liked tradition,
which I think is why

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.452
I haven't minded that I haven't
spent Christmas with family.

00:05:49.452 --> 00:05:51.462
Cause I started my own traditions.

00:05:51.462 --> 00:05:53.195
I usually spend it with friends.

00:05:53.195 --> 00:05:55.186
- Yeah in the long run, I
think holidays are such a small

00:05:55.186 --> 00:05:58.056
part of what it is to be a family.

00:05:58.056 --> 00:06:00.058
I wouldn't say I'm jaded
about the holidays,

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:02.188
like, I think it's appropriate
to call me a grinch

00:06:02.188 --> 00:06:05.660
or whatever, but, there
are so many other moments

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:09.733
to share with my family,
that Christmas or Easter,

00:06:09.733 --> 00:06:11.835
or whatever isn't really the biggest part

00:06:11.835 --> 00:06:13.724
that I feel bringing us together.

00:06:13.724 --> 00:06:15.919
- Oh yeah, I think that
everything I've said

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:17.860
wouldn't offend my mom, so that's good.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.610
- [Interviewer] That's a relief.

